## Semantic Builder → IR Lowering (SemanticBuilder.cs - IRBuilder method)

For each bound statement, emit IR:

**INITIATE report-name:**
- Per reportName:
  - Call IrRuntimeCall("ReportRuntime.InitializeReport", [reportName_str, fileConnector_ref])
  - This runtime method: sets LINE-COUNTER=0, PAGE-COUNTER=1, zeros all SUM counters, saves prior controls

**GENERATE detail-name | report-name:**
- Call IrRuntimeCall("ReportRuntime.GenerateReport", [reportName_str, detailName_str, fileHandle])
- Runtime method: (see ReportWriterRuntime class below)
  1. If first GENERATE: print REPORT HEADING + first PAGE HEADING + all CONTROL HEADINGS (major→minor)
  2. Detect control breaks (compare current CONTROL items against prior controls)
  3. If break detected: print CONTROL FOOTINGs (minor→major) then CONTROL HEADINGs (major→minor)
  4. Perform page fit test: if detail won't fit, page advance (FOOTER, PAGE COUNTER++, LINE-COUNTER=0, HEADER)
  5. Format and position detail fields (LINE NUMBER absolute/relative/NEXT PAGE, COLUMN NUMBER)
  6. Accumulate SUM counters (if UPON this detail)
  7. Emit IrWriteReportLine to write the formatted line
  8. Update LINE-COUNTER after write

**TERMINATE report-name:**
- Call IrRuntimeCall("ReportRuntime.TerminateReport", [reportName_str, fileHandle])
- Runtime method:
  1. If no GENERATE executed: just mark inactive, return
  2. If GENERATEs executed: save current control values, restore priors
  3. Print all CONTROL FOOTINGs (minor→major) as if major-level break
  4. Print REPORT FOOTING
  5. Restore control values to current (post-break)
  6. Mark report inactive

